// @emit-error value-call union-ARM parameter given a value that is not that arm
// THE THIRD SHAPE THE FLOOR NAMED AND NO FILE HELD. `arm-param-value-call-box-arg-floor.vl`
// listed three programs that reach `emitCallRef`'s missing `variant`-parameter arm — an
// un-annotated binding that reps as the BOX, a bare object LITERAL argument, and an
// `is`-NARROWED union binding — and pinned only the first while the second got its own
// file. The first graduated to `@run` when D244 stopped the producer repping as the box,
// so this one exists to keep the floor's coverage from shrinking with it.
//
// A NARROWED `s` is still the `{tag, value}` BOX at the call: the narrow proves WHICH arm
// rides the payload, it does not re-rep the binding. `emitCallRef` has a `union`-parameter
// arm and no `variant`-parameter one, so without the floor the box goes raw into a
// `(ref $uVarHeap[Circle])` slot — check-clean INVALID WASM, which is the outcome a floor
// exists to keep loud. D200's second witness is the row; flip this file to `@run` when the
// value call learns to unbox against the declared arm.
//
// NO LAYOUT TWIN, deliberately: `Circle` is the only `{r: i32}` in the program, so the
// disguise cannot come from a struct scan matching a same-shape row.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
const lamc = (x: Circle) => x
function m3(s: Shape) { if s is Circle { lamc(s).r } else { 0 } }
print(m3({ r: 7 }))
